    "updated_at": "2016-03-23T10:10:35Z",
    "body": "Since a lot of media processing doesn't happen on the same thread as JS execution, it makes more sense to express this in terms of the process that happens to produce the pixels on the screen.  Binding this back to actions in script-land doesn't make sense.  Also, I expect that microtasks won't fit, since anything happening off-thread will want to queue a task to communicate back with JS.\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
