    "created_at": "2016-03-24T14:49:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-24T14:49:43Z",
    "body": "Maybe I am not using the exact right wording with \"for each element in the document\". A canvas that is not attached to the DOM still has an ownerDocument. For example, when you call myDocument.createElement('canvas'), the new canvas is not in any DOM, but it is still owned by myDocument. If I am not mistaken all nodes except for Document nodes always have a non-null ownerDocument. Would it be more accurate to say \"for each element owned by the document\"?\n\nRegarding HTMLCanvasElement::notifyListenersCanvasChanged in Blink, we call it during blink's paint invalidation phase which is a part of the rendering update that we perform on the main thread. It maps to step 7.12 of the even loop processing model.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
