    "created_at": "2018-01-29T21:08:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-01-29T21:08:32Z",
    "body": "annevk@ that is mostly defined in the current spec already, see methods section in https://w3c.github.io/mediacapture-fromelement/#html-canvas-element-media-capture-extensions. i.e. the references where hook is called are referred as \"each track capturing from the canvas\". I think the ambiguous part, as pointed in the first post, is this reference: \"A new frame is requested from the canvas when frameCaptureRequested is true and the canvas is painted.\" If we have the proposed change in the event loop processing model 7.12, we can refer to that instead of \"painted\". Also, we can clarify exactly when that new frame is added to the MediaStreamTrack in relation to the event. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
